  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "A country welcomed $3,\\,500,\\,000$ tourists in $2018.$  Travel authorities predict that this number will increase by $45%$ by the year $2028.$ Which of the following is closest to the projected number of tourists in $2028?$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the projected number of tourists in $2028,$ we apply a $45%$ increase to the $2018$ figure.\n\nIncreasing by $45%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+45%=145%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n145%=\\frac{145}{100}=1.45\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the new value by multiplying the original amount by $1.45:$\n\n$$\n3,\\,500,\\,000\\times 1.45=5,\\,075,\\,000\n$$\n\nTherefore, the projected number of tourists in $2028$ is $5,\\,075,\\,000.$",
